    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d374">

                <pb facs="1067" n="1881" xml:id="pg1881"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/S–NSC files, lot 66 D 95, “Jackson
                    Committee”</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum for the National Security Council by the
                        Executive Secretary (Lay)</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d374-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-10-01">October 1, 1953</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <item>Subject:</item>
                    <item>Progress Report on Implementation of the Recommendations of the Jackson
                            Committee<anchor n="2" xml:id="d374-f2"/></item>
                </list>
                <list rendition="#flush" type="references">
                    <head>References:</head>
                    <label>A.</label>
                    <item>NSC Action No. 866<anchor n="3" xml:id="d374-f3"/></item>
                    <label>B.</label>
                    <item>Memo for NSC from Executive Secretary, subject “Report by the President’s
                        Committee on International Information Activities dated June 30, 1953
                        (except Chapter 7)” dated July 20, 1953<anchor n="4" xml:id="d374-f4"
                        /></item>
                </list>
                <p>The enclosed progress report by the Operations Coordinating Board on
                    implementation of the recommendations of the Jackson Committee report referred
                    to in subparagraphs 2 c and d of the reference memorandum is transmitted
                    herewith for the information of the National Security Council and will be
                    scheduled on the agenda of an early Council meeting.<anchor n="5"
                        xml:id="d374-f5"/></p>
                <p>In accordance with the request of the Director of Central Intelligence Annexes E
                    and F<anchor n="6" xml:id="d374-f6"/> of the report, containing “Eyes Only”
                    material, are included only in a very limited number of the copies of the report
                    which are being distributed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Lay, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>








                <xi:include href="d374-a1.xml" xpointer="d374-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d374-a2.xml" xpointer="d374-a2"/>
