        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d374-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d374-f1-content">
                <p>Copies also sent to the Secretary of the Treasury, the Director of the Bureau of
                    the Budget, the Director of the U.S. Information Agency, the Chairman of the
                    Joint Chiefs of Staff, and the Director of Central Intelligence.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d374-f2" n="2" xml:id="d374-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the Jackson Committee Report, June 30, see <ref target="#pg1795">p.
                        1795</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d374-f3" n="3" xml:id="d374-f3-content">
                <p>In NSC Action No. 866, taken by the Council at its 157th meeting, July 30, 1953,
                    the NSC approved the recommendations of the Planning Board contained in the
                    memorandum by Executive Secretary Lay of July 20, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >supra</hi>. (S/S–NSC files, lot 66 D 95, “NSC Records of Action”)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d374-f4" n="4" xml:id="d374-f4-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d374-f5" n="5" xml:id="d374-f5-content">
                <p>At its 167th meeting, Oct. 22, 1953, the National Security Council noted this
                    progress report. (S/S–NSC files, lot 66 D 95, “NSC Records of Action”)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d374-f6" n="6" xml:id="d374-f6-content">
                <p>Annex F is not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
